{"id": "karhutla", "kind": "pemerintah · defensif", "account": "Akun resmi sebuah kementerian", "subject": "the government's handling of the 2026 forest and peat fires (karhutla) and the haze", "recorded": "2026-10-30", "episodes": [{"text": "Titik api turun 60% dalam sepekan. Satgas bekerja 24 jam, sisa 639 hektare sedang ditangani. Kabut asap lintas batas bukan hanya dari Indonesia. Mohon tidak menyebarkan foto lama dan hoaks. #SiagaKarhutla", "result": {"text": "Titik api turun 60% dalam sepekan. Satgas bekerja 24 jam, sisa 639 hektare sedang ditangani. Kabut asap lintas batas bukan hanya dari Indonesia. Mohon tidak menyebarkan foto lama dan hoaks. #SiagaKarhutla", "context": "Forest and peat fires (karhutla) have burned since July 2026 (about 95,000 hectares in July alone); Kalimantan and Sumatra have breathed toxic haze for four months, worst on 13-15 October, with schools closed and ojol and street vendors losing income. Malaysia and Singapore protested the cross-border haze, a class action is being prepared, and NGOs, clerics and regional leaders demand national-disaster status, which the government has not granted. President Prabowo said he hoped for rain, which netizens mocked ('then what is the government for?'); a governor went viral having a lavish breakfast abroad during the haze, and influencers complained Instagram throttled their karhutla posts. The dominant narrative: the government lets corporate land burn and understates the crisis.", "tokens": 324750, "segments": ["s_traveler"], "anchors": [{"id": "c4_pagar_laut", "similarity": 1.7, "mix": {"negative": 0.16989737742303307, "neutral": 0.14139110604332952, "positive": 0.6887115165336374}, "n": 877}, {"id": "c1_ppn12", "similarity": 0.97, "mix": {"negative": 0.6340057636887608, "neutral": 0.2680115273775216, "positive": 0.09798270893371758}, "n": 694}, {"id": "c5_efisiensi", "similarity": 0.92, "mix": {"negative": 0.3453333333333333, "neutral": 0.15333333333333332, "positive": 0.5013333333333333}, "